    "body": "### Is your proposal related to a problem?\r\n\r\nSome users want to auto-delete their post and/or comments after a period of time to avoid potential brigading, stalking, doxxing and other abuse.\r\n\r\n### Describe the solution you'd like\r\n\r\nA compromise between content deletion for privacy reasons and maintaining content for the community:\r\n\r\n**_Allow posts to be anonymized after a period of time._**\r\n\r\nThis should be opt-in. The time limit before content anonymization could be set by the developers to maintain a universal standard, by the instance admins or the users themselves. There should be a warning for inexperienced users that this only deletes content on the lemmy network and does not \"scrub\" it from the internet.\r\n\r\n### Describe alternatives you've considered\r\n\r\n- Manually deleting comments and posts\r\n- Using scripts like on reddit\r\n- Not using lemmy or social media for privacy reasons\r\n\r\n### Additional context\r\n\r\nOriginal discussion\r\nhttps://github.com/LemmyNet/lemmy/issues/2415\r\n",
